  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pacific Community (SPC) and Government of Australia Partnership (2021-2023)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Pacific Community (SPC) is the premier provider of regional technical and scientific assistance to developing countries in the Pacific. This investment is part of the ten-year SPC-Government of Australia Partnership that sets out how SPC and Australia will work together to address major regional development issues in line with SPC&apos;s mandate. The Partnership provides the mechanism through which all Australian ODA funds are governed and guides the way in which all Australian Government stakeholders work with SPC. This will provide greater coherence across the broad spectrum of Australian Government engagement with SPC.</narrative>
  </description>
